/* book exam traps: z₁₁ is measured with port 2 open, not shorted. For the T network, shorting port 2 gives 3.7143 Ω, not z₁₁ = 6 Ω; 3.7143 Ω is 1/y₁₁. | z₁₂ is not 1/y₁₂. Here z₁₂ = 4 Ω but 1/y₁₂ = 1/(−0.1538) = −6.5 Ω. Invert the whole matrix. | The off-diagonal terms change sign in the inversion: y₁₂ = −z₁₂/Δz. Writing +z₁₂/Δz gives y₂₁ = +0.1538 S, which says current enters terminal 2 from the short, which is impossible for a passive network driven at port 1. | Units: z in ohms, y in siemens, Δz in Ω², Δy in S². A determinant written in plain ohms is marked wrong. | Not every network has both sets: a lone series element has no Z matrix and a lone shunt element has no Y matrix. */
